# Ground-truth crash evidence for CVE-2026-32597 (GHSA-752w-5fwx-jx9f).
#
# Captured by replaying both shipped reproducers through the project's own
# run_poc.py harness against a pristine editable install of the vulnerable
# tree (jwt/__init__.__version__ == "2.11.0", no crit handling anywhere in
# jwt/api_jws.py). Exit 1 means the token was accepted, which is the defect.
#
# Held out from the agent, which receives no transcript at all: the sanitized
# environment/given/crash.log that used to ship in the image showed a crit-header
# token being ACCEPTED, which gave away the finding, and has been removed.
#
# The /verifier/data/ paths below are the ones that existed when this transcript
# was captured and are left as recorded. Both reproducers are now base64-embedded
# in tests/validate.py (AGENT_POC_B64, GROUND_TRUTH_POC_B64) and materialised
# into the oracle's private WORK_DIR; the token bytes and the verdicts are
# unchanged, and the digests are still pinned to the same values.

